# Project Principles

This is a short index of stable cross-cutting engineering rules. It is not a broad project manual.

## What Belongs Here

- durable repo-wide principles
- doc ownership boundaries
- planning and context-hygiene defaults

## Core Principles

1. Keep docs layered instead of centralizing everything into one manual.
2. Keep every repo-changing task resumable from `PLANS.md`.
3. Keep active work in `PLANS.md` and inactive future work in `docs/codex/TASKS_BACKLOG.md`.
4. Compact or archive completed plan detail when it stops helping active or imminent work.
5. Keep recurring mistakes in `docs/codex/AGENT_EXECUTION_PITFALLS.md` until they become durable principles.
6. Keep passing noise out of the working context.
